                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4f8da052-7d28-380a-b9a2-0e3477304ed5",
                        "entry_id": "d72526fa-1454-386b-ab87-8e665aef352f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "übermäßig vorteilhafte Darstellung der Polizei in PR-Aktionen, Nachrichten oder fiktionalen Medien, wie Serien oder Filmen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88ed86ee-3854-4adc-9017-84694c87b2aa",
                                "sense_id": "4f8da052-7d28-380a-b9a2-0e3477304ed5",
                                "text": "„Copaganda ist ein Phänomen, das sowohl in der US-Unterhaltungsindustrie, aber auch in Deutschland Millionen von Menschen in ihrer Sicht auf die Polizei stark beeinflusst.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "26c7efe6-0ce4-451b-90d4-20af4cbd8901",
                                "sense_id": "4f8da052-7d28-380a-b9a2-0e3477304ed5",
                                "text": "„Die Serie wurde einerseits immer sehr gelobt – sie ist divers besetzt, die Figuren sind gegen Klischees gebürstet –, aber andererseits betreibt sie eben Copaganda, also macht Werbung für die Agenda von Polizisten.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca5c07b2-9ca2-44f2-bab6-1fbddd0e949c",
                                "sense_id": "4f8da052-7d28-380a-b9a2-0e3477304ed5",
                                "text": "„Und dazu gelingt es hier, eine Polizei-Geschichte zu erzählen, ohne dabei Copaganda (die Glorifizierung von Polizei-Arbeit) zu betreiben.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92bfc966-1f52-45fb-9609-eb91d2d28cf3",
                                "sense_id": "4f8da052-7d28-380a-b9a2-0e3477304ed5",
                                "text": "„Doch die «Zootopia»-Moral, «Gib dir Mühe und hilf', durch Weltoffenheit die ganze Welt zu ändern: Geh doch zum Beispiel zur Polizei!», ist «Copaganda».“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aa8b1bb6-833d-42a2-9e92-d9d22c95ca9b",
                        "source_entry_id": "d72526fa-1454-386b-ab87-8e665aef352f",
                        "source_sense_id": "4f8da052-7d28-380a-b9a2-0e3477304ed5",
                        "source_sense_description": "übermäßig vorteilhafte Darstellung der Polizei",
                        "target_lang_word": "copaganda",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "copaganda",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                        "entry_id": "3fe13279-1f09-36af-8989-1e5b9f090f88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Media that contains messages seen as propaganda in favor of the police."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "321ed195-d941-43b3-ba5a-07bfc4b676bf",
                                                "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                                "text": "Mostly Hollywood has simply churned out malignant copaganda that glamorizes police brutality and normalizes the idea that the only good cop is a bad cop."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7b6611c-9168-46d9-8292-f2bc6588bd69",
                                                "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                                "text": "Sick of all these Copaganda shows on TV. Are these the same cops that hide in vans every weekend and take 45 mins to respond to 999 calls?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ca75af6-ee56-4588-a7af-efa06dd4c677",
                                                "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                                "text": "That David Simon could tell people with bricks in their hand to “go home,” and have no direct words of condemnation for the violence displayed by the police made me remember my friend Dashon — from Baltimore — who told me he would never watch The Wire because he believed it to be “copaganda,” since it was created not only by Simon but by longtime Baltimore police officer Ed Burns."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc83e08c-42ae-4c29-8d27-5e4817257411",
                                                "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                                "text": "To counter this, police reform and police abolitionist activists on Twitter have invented a rather useful term: \"Copaganda.\" Copaganda is any news story that uncritically advances a police department's image or helps undermine reform efforts. Here are eight of the most common forms of copaganda."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a63549f0-0bcf-4f35-8e7a-5fe61c312c13",
                                                "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                                "text": "However, while an article about Robert Downey Jr. visiting a child dying of leukemia doesn’t have an impact on the public perception of criminal justice, copaganda does."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75a006ad-bc61-4519-857c-77eb1d3e4618",
                                                "sense_id": "6e8d24d7-40df-3fdf-8a44-26f58e5374c8",
                                                "text": "“Yeah, wading down into the comments. \"Winsomely compelling cop-aganda,\" says C-Rob-69. Oh, wait, that was me.” “Drivel for the unwashed. The Bard, how he weeps.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
